#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0528 expect=violation domain=SUPPDM
#note "Row 1: the ADSL population flag SAFETY as a DM supplemental qualifier, RDOMAIN = dm (lower case) -> violation; row 2 is an ordinary qualifier. Rule round 2026-10-12 (owner, queued item C3, as c5206c02): RDOMAIN names a domain, and dataset names match case-insensitively (owner 2026-10-01), so the literal comparison reads upper(RDOMAIN). Red under the old exact comparison (no finding)."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 QNAM=SAFETY
dataset SUPPDM label="Supplemental Qualifiers"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col RDOMAIN  type=Char label="Related Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col IDVAR    type=Char label="Identifying Variable"
col IDVARVAL type=Char label="Identifying Variable Value"
col QNAM     type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Name"
col QLABEL   type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Label"
col QVAL     type=Char label="Data Value"
---
S1 | dm | 001 |  |  | SAFETY | Safety Population | Y
S1 | dm | 001 |  |  | RACEOTH | Race, Other | ASIAN-INDIAN
